{
  "summary": "This experiment tested the effect of upgrading the image encoder from ResNet50 to imagenet_vit_l while holding all other settings (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool, weighted fusion) constant relative to llm_summary_008, yielding a validation accuracy of 0.706 (F1 0.667) versus 0.678 (F1 0.646) for ResNet50. Because only the image encoder changed, this clean single-variable comparison indicates that the image channel's contribution was partially encoder-limited: the stronger ViT-L backbone unlocks approximately 2.9 additional accuracy points of complementary signal, bringing the total multimodal gain over the RNA-only multiprofile baseline (0.650, llm_summary_004) to roughly 5.6 points. It remains uncertain whether further encoder scaling, alternative fusion strategies, or additional tuning could extract more signal from the image modality, or whether the current configuration is approaching the achievable ceiling for this task."
}

